acklog of cases uh in our country's  history even before the pandemic hits  there were now sixty thousand cases  waiting waiting in the courts to be  heard for a rape case now you wait three  years uh to cart to come to trial and  that's if you're one of the one and a  half percent of reported rapes that ever  gets to trial in the first place so the  criminal justice system is absolutely  broken because of what the government's  done now nobody wants to see a strike  making that even even worse barristers  you know with their gowns and their wigs  and not a naturally militant group of  people they've never gone on strike  before but they're striking because of  the disarray and the Justice uh in the  in the criminal justice system and  frankly because the government went back  on the commitments they made to properly  fund uh properly fund legal aid a piece  of work that they commissioned and that  was written by a conservative a  conservative peer now what Dominique  robber whoever becomes Justice secretary  secretary could do is sit down with a  Criminal Bar Association that represents  barristers and try to talk through the  problems they've said on each occasion  this year when they've held a ballot on  Industrial action they've said if  Dominic Rob will the Justice secretary  sat down and spoke with them they would  call off the action if I was the Justice  secretary that is what I would do  frankly we have a zombie government in  so many respects but one way that they  can help with these strikes is simply to  talk to the uh to the barristers and  perhaps try to keep their word on the  legal aid funding program which they  first of all said in the House of  Commons they would support but then went  back on okay and finally then Steve I  mean if the reporting is correct and it  seems to be pretty accurate and this  trust does win the leadership racing  comes our next prime minister uh who she  suggested to be in her cabinet looks  like being one of the most diverse  cabinets in history and of course it  will be the conservative party's third  prime minister the labor party haven't  even had a female leader you must be a  little bit jealous of the way that the  conservative party seems to have a  diverse top team in place well Kamali we  we don't actually know who's won yet let  alone who would be  um in their cabinets so that's so that's  a that's a bit of speculation but I'll  tell you what really matters what really  matters to the British people is what  they do not what they are and right now  the biggest crisis facing our country is  the is the escalating energy bills  Labor's got a fully costed plan soon I  can trust have both said nothing about  what they would do the country needs  help now that requires a real fresh  start which neither of these two can  give only a labor Government Can can  deliver that

